SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"IMF Staff Visit Discusses Reform Plans and Economic Developments in Ethiopia","publisher":"IMF","publication_date":"2022-06-21","url":"https://www.imf.org/en/news/articles/2022/06/21/pr22216-ethiopia-imf-staff-visit-discusses-reform-plans-and-economic-developments-in-ethiopia","claim":"The IMF said Ethiopia's authorities aimed to address macroeconomic imbalances, remain committed to structural reforms for a transition to private sector-led growth, and advance debt treatment, FX reforms, and monetary-policy modernization.","locator":"press release body and quoted statements on reform plans","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary IMF staff-visit release with direct statements about the government's 2022 reform agenda and the constraints it faced.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within 2022; describes the government's 2022 reform agenda and implementation constraints.","ruler_attribution":"Attributed to Abiy Ahmed's government through the IMF mission's meetings with Ethiopian authorities and the stated reform agenda; it shows declared program and policy direction, not full execution proof.","contrary_evidence":["The same release says growth was hit by multiple shocks, inflation, FX shortages, and fiscal/external pressure."],"lenses":["8B.1","8B.2","8B.6","8B.7","8B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Strong Monitoring, Evaluation Mechanism Key to Effective Utilization of Draft Budget: Planning and Development Minister","publisher":"ENA","publication_date":"2022-06-18","url":"https://www.ena.et/web/eng/w/en_36589","claim":"The draft 2022/23 budget was said to be aligned with the 10-year development plan, and the planning minister stressed that strong monitoring and evaluation were critical to ensure implementation and impact evaluation.","locator":"report body, especially the minister's interview on monitoring and plan alignment","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Government news agency reporting a ministerial interview about the implementation apparatus for the budget and plan.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exactly within the 2022 budget cycle.","ruler_attribution":"Attributed to Abiy's administration through the planning minister and the Council of Ministers' budget submission; it shows operational design, not guaranteed delivery.","contrary_evidence":["The source is an implementation claim by a government outlet and does not independently verify execution quality."],"lenses":["8B.2","8B.6","8B.8"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"House Approves Over 786 Billion Birr Budget for Ethiopian FY","publisher":"ENA","publication_date":"2022-07-07","url":"https://www.ena.et/web/eng/w/en_37020","claim":"Ethiopia's 2022/23 federal budget was approved at 786.6 billion birr and explicitly prioritized debt payment, humanitarian assistance, rehabilitation and reconstruction, displaced people, security forces, ongoing projects, and damaged infrastructure and services.","locator":"budget approval report body","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Government news agency reporting the approved budget and its stated spending priorities.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in 2022, covering the new fiscal year's budget.","ruler_attribution":"Attributed to Abiy's government because the House approved the cabinet-submitted budget and the report describes the administration's priorities; it does not by itself prove outcomes.","contrary_evidence":["Conflict and debt pressure constrained the fiscal room available to the government."],"lenses":["8B.2","8B.6","8B.9"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Gov't to Focus on Fiscal Consolidation in New Ethiopia Budget Year","publisher":"ENA","publication_date":"2022-07-07","url":"https://www.ena.et/web/eng/w/en_37023","claim":"Abiy said the new budget year would prioritize fiscal consolidation, higher poverty-alleviation spending, lower reliance on bank credit, inflation control, productivity gains, and reconstruction/humanitarian support.","locator":"PM remarks in the budget report","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct government reporting of the prime minister's budget remarks and stated policy priorities.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exactly within 2022 budget-year planning.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to Abiy as head of government and speaker on the budget; it shows the program he said he was steering.","contrary_evidence":["The same report says inflation was already high and debt/deficit pressures remained serious."],"lenses":["8B.2","8B.6","8B.7","8B.8"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Gov't Establishes National Committee To Coordinate Anti-Corruption Campaign","publisher":"ENA","publication_date":"2022-11-17","url":"https://www.ena.et/web/eng/w/en_40240","claim":"Abiy announced a national anti-corruption committee to coordinate the campaign, investigate officials and bribe givers/takers, and bring corrupt actors before court.","locator":"report body and PM statement on forming the committee","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct government announcement of a new enforcement mechanism and its stated mandate.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Within 2022 and directly tied to the anti-corruption drive.","ruler_attribution":"Strongly attributable to Abiy because he announced the committee and described its purpose; it shows adaptive response to an identified problem, not proven success.","contrary_evidence":["The announcement itself is a promise of action, not evidence that corruption was actually reduced."],"lenses":["8B.3","8B.5","8B.8","8B.9"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Nat'l Anti-Corruption Committee Detaining Suspects for Corrupt Practices","publisher":"ENA","publication_date":"2022-12-02","url":"https://www.ena.et/web/eng/w/en_40822","claim":"The anti-corruption committee said it had begun arresting suspects, including officials tied to financial plundering and land grabbing, and identified additional corruption cases in Addis Ababa and other sectors.","locator":"committee briefing report body","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Government news agency reporting a concrete enforcement step shortly after the committee was created.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Within 2022 and following the November anti-corruption announcement.","ruler_attribution":"Attributable to Abiy's administration because the committee was government-established and reported arrests under its mandate; independent verification of case quality is limited.","contrary_evidence":["The report does not independently verify the cases or show the long-term effectiveness of the crackdown."],"lenses":["8B.6","8B.8","8B.9","8B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"National Peace Council Established","publisher":"ENA","publication_date":"2022-11-28","url":"https://www.ena.et/web/eng/w/en_40598","claim":"A National Peace Council was established to support lasting peace in Ethiopia, coordinate peacebuilding, and support the National Dialogue Commission with participation from religious institutions, civil society, security bodies, higher-education institutions, intellectuals, and political parties.","locator":"launch report body","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Official reporting on the creation and membership of a new peace-coordination institution.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Within 2022 and directly tied to peace and dialogue implementation.","ruler_attribution":"Attributed to Abiy's governing network because the council was created by the government to operationalize the peace process; the report does not prove downstream results.","contrary_evidence":["The same period still had contested dialogue politics and incomplete reconciliation."],"lenses":["8B.3","8B.5","8B.9","8B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Ethiopia says Tigray aid allowed, agencies say still no access","publisher":"Reuters via Euronews","publication_date":"2022-11-12","url":"https://www.euronews.com/2022/11/12/ethiopia-conflict-aid","claim":"After the Nov. 2 ceasefire, the Ethiopian government said aid was allowed and ready to move into Tigray, but humanitarian agencies said they were still waiting for access and only 35 government aid trucks had reached Shire.","locator":"Reuters story body on aid access and implementation talks","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters reporting is independent and directly contemporaneous, with clear attribution to government and humanitarian actors.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Within 2022 and immediately after the ceasefire agreement.","ruler_attribution":"Attributed to Abiy's government because the government controlled access and implementation; the same report shows the limits of implementation at that point.","contrary_evidence":["Humanitarian agencies said access was still blocked or incomplete, so the implementation was only partial."],"lenses":["8B.6","8B.8","8B.9","8B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Ethiopia's Abiy vows 'honest' implementation of Tigray truce","publisher":"Reuters via Euronews","publication_date":"2022-11-16","url":"https://www.euronews.com/2022/11/16/ethiopia-conflict","claim":"Abiy told parliament he would implement the ceasefire honestly and said the truce was needed so peace would be sustainable.","locator":"Reuters story on parliamentary remarks","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Independent Reuters report of a direct parliamentary statement by the prime minister.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Within 2022, shortly after the ceasefire agreement.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable as Abiy's own public commitment, but it is a promise rather than proof of execution.","contrary_evidence":["The statement itself does not prove implementation, and other reporting still described access and service-restoration gaps."],"lenses":["8B.1","8B.6","8B.9","8B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Ethiopia kicks off a nationwide integrated measles vaccination campaign targeting over 15.5 million children","publisher":"WHO Regional Office for Africa","publication_date":"2022-12-30","url":"https://www.afro.who.int/fr/node/17139","claim":"Ethiopia's Ministry of Health launched a nationwide integrated measles vaccination campaign targeting 15.5 million children, including hard-to-reach drought- and conflict-affected areas, with WHO support and deployment of more than 100 experts.","locator":"campaign launch article body","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"WHO regional office report on a concrete government-led health campaign with partner support and implementation details.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within late 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Attributed to Abiy's administration through the Ministry of Health's launch of the campaign; the campaign also relied heavily on partners, so attribution is shared.","contrary_evidence":["The need for a massive catch-up campaign shows existing immunity gaps in conflict- and drought-affected areas."],"lenses":["8B.6","8B.8","8B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"The Government of Ethiopia is Delivering on its Commitment to Restoring Services across Tigray Region","publisher":"Embassy of the Federal Democratic Republic of Ethiopia, London / APO Group","publication_date":"2022-12-30","url":"https://www.africa-newsroom.com/press/the-government-of-ethiopia-is-delivering-on-its-commitment-to-restoring-services-across-tigray-region?lang=en","claim":"The government reported restoring key services in Tigray, including reconnecting eight power substations, bringing 65 telecom stations into operation, repairing 981 km of fiber, and reopening 61 bank branches.","locator":"press release body on service restoration figures","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Official embassy press release distributed through APO with concrete restoration numbers, though still a government self-report.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within 2022 and describing post-ceasefire implementation.","ruler_attribution":"Attributed to Abiy's government because the service restoration was presented as implementation of the federal ceasefire commitment; external corroboration is still preferable for full confidence.","contrary_evidence":["The report says restoration was partial and still unfolding, not complete across all of Tigray."],"lenses":["8B.6","8B.9","8B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Aid access to Ethiopia's Tigray continues to open up: UN","publisher":"Xinhua / UN OCHA reporting","publication_date":"2022-12-16","url":"https://english.news.cn/20221216/cd751f95c0a1406cb127fc4bd8517b86c/c.html","claim":"UN humanitarians said aid access to Tigray was gradually opening up, with the government and partners mobilizing more than 1,600 trucks delivering food and other supplies through four corridors between Nov. 15 and Dec. 8.","locator":"UN/OCHA quoted section in the story body","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"The article relays UN humanitarian figures and timing, giving a concrete independent check on the reopening of access.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Within 2022 and directly about post-ceasefire implementation.","ruler_attribution":"Shared attribution: the government's opening of access mattered, but UN and partner logistics also drove the result; this is implementation evidence rather than exclusive ruler credit.","contrary_evidence":["The report says access was only gradually opening, which means the humanitarian response remained incomplete."],"lenses":["8B.6","8B.9","8B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"World Leaders Archive: Ethiopia","publisher":"CIA","publication_date":"2022-08-24","url":"https://www.cia.gov/resources/world-leaders/historical-data/2022-september/ethiopia","claim":"The 2022 cabinet roster lists Abiy Ahmed as prime minister and Ahmed Shide as finance minister, with Fitsum Assefa and other ministers in the cabinet.","locator":"country leader page / cabinet roster","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Official U.S. government leader roster provides a contemporaneous snapshot of cabinet composition.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Within 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Shows the staffing Abiy controlled, but it does not by itself prove capability or execution quality.","contrary_evidence":["Cabinet composition alone does not show whether the appointees were effective."],"lenses":["8B.4"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Ahmed Shide","publisher":"World Bank Live","publication_date":"unknown","url":"https://live.worldbank.org/en/experts/a/ahmed-shide","claim":"Ahmed Shide is described as having served as Ethiopia's finance minister since October 2018 and having prior finance-ministry experience, indicating a technocratic background relevant to economic implementation.","locator":"biographical profile","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official World Bank profile with a specific career history relevant to economic administration.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Background context that was already in force during 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Relevant because Abiy retained Shide in the finance portfolio; it supports an inference of experienced personnel, but not a direct measure of outcomes.","contrary_evidence":["A biography shows experience, not that the government's economic program succeeded."],"lenses":["8B.4"]}

**Search And Rejection Summary**
I screened roughly 30 documents across IMF, ENA, Reuters/Euronews, AP/PBS, WHO, UN/Xinhua, World Bank, CIA, Addis Standard, The New Humanitarian, CPJ, Access Now, Freedom House, HRW, and a few registry-style pages.

Kept or reused:
- IMF and ENA budget/plan documents for the 2022 reform program, budget priorities, and implementation machinery.
- Reuters, AP/embassy, WHO, and UN/Xinhua for concrete post-ceasefire and service-restoration implementation.
- ENA anti-corruption and peace-council items for adaptation, coordination, and follow-through.
- CIA and World Bank Live for cabinet/staffing context.

Rejected or downgraded:
- Duplicate humanitarian-access stories from UNHCR/WFP/UNICEF and repeated Reuters/AP updates where the same factual core appeared in more than one outlet.
- Pure context indicators and country-level macro series that were useful as priors but not ruler-specific 8B evidence.
- Rights/media-crackdown sources that were more relevant to 1B/3B/4B than 8B, unless they also showed program execution or state control.
- Out-of-period 2023-2024 material was screened but not needed because 2022 sources already established the program and implementation chain.
- The PolicyVault asset-disclosure page was blocked by robots and was not needed once the other 2022 sources covered planning, execution, and adaptation.

**Remaining Gaps**
- I still do not have an independent audit of 2022 budget execution, so the budget/plan evidence is stronger on priorities than on verified delivery.
- Economic effectiveness remains partially clouded by conflict, drought, inflation, FX shortages, and debt pressure; the record shows ambition and some implementation, but not clean outcome attribution.
- Appointment evidence is still thin beyond the finance/planning portfolio; I do not yet have a full, ruler-attributed map of sectoral competence across the cabinet and regional machinery.
- The anti-corruption drive is visible in announcements and initial arrests, but not in independent case-level outcomes or durable institutional change.
- More search would help if you want tighter evidence on budget execution, National Bank policy actions, procurement/audit findings, or post-agreement restoration metrics across more sectors.
